# Git commits: no Cursor co-author

- **Never** put `Co-authored-by: Cursor` (or any Cursor / cursoragent trailer) in commit messages.
- When creating commits, use only the real author identity already configured for this repo.
- If a commit message template or tool injects a Cursor co-author line, **strip it before committing**.
- Do **not** use `git commit --amend` solely to add Cursor attribution.
- Prefer: `git commit -F <msgfile>` where the file has no Cursor trailer.

## Bad

```
Release 0.4.1: fix Flash Search page load.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

## Good

```
Release 0.4.1: fix Flash Search page load.

Remove invalid Md3TextField onEditingFinished handler that prevented the page from loading.
```

Repo hooks under `.githooks/` strip/reject Cursor co-author trailers. After clone: `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`
